1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:02,132
The microwave beeps.

2
00:00:02,232 --> 00:00:04,267
It's done — but your food isn't.

3
00:00:04,633 --> 00:00:07,834
In thick food, the waves mostly heat the outer layers.

4
00:00:07,934 --> 00:00:12,367
When they stop, the outside is hot — the middle is still catching up.

5
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:18,433
That heat keeps flowing inward, from the hot outside to the cooler center — no microwaves needed.

6
00:00:18,833 --> 00:00:20,146
That's standing time.

7
00:00:20,246 --> 00:00:25,467
Food keeps cooking after the oven stops — its temperature can climb several more degrees.

8
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:25,833
It's not extra heating.

9
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:29,633
It's the same heat, spreading out.

10
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:35,300
Food-safety guides say let it stand at least three minutes — then check it with a food thermometer.

11
00:00:35,767 --> 00:00:37,626
The beep means the waves are done.

12
00:00:37,726 --> 00:00:40,267
Standing time lets the heat finish the job.
